# Multiplier in Conway's register style: 2^a * 3^b -> 5^(a*b).
# Registers: 2 holds a (decremented once per outer pass), 3 holds b
# (moved back and forth), 5 accumulates the product. Primes 7, 11, 13 are
# state markers: 11 marks "copying b into 5 and 7", 13 relays 7 back into 3
# via 11, 7 holds the saved copy of b between passes.
# A standard register-machine construction in the style of Conway's paper
# (circulating widely, e.g. on the esolangs wiki); verified against this
# interpreter for a range of inputs.
# Run: lake exe fractran --n 108 --out final multiply.ft   (2^2 * 3^3 -> 5^6 = 15625)

455/33 11/13 1/11 3/7 11/2 1/3
